          "code_snippet": " handler until the store recovers, so use it only for idempotent handlers. And `payment_replayed` means the authorization was presented before, not that the first attempt failed: if the client lost the first response, the work may have run and the payment may have settled, so it should reconcile the original request before signing a new authorization. This closes duplicate copies of one authorization only. A payer who invalidates the payment between verify and settle (for example by moving the funds) still gets one handler run; for expensive routes, hold funds before doing the work.\n\n**Discovery.** Facilitators that implement the x402 bazaar extension expose a `/discovery/resources` endpoint \u2014 query the CDP catalog at `https://api.cdp.coinbase.com/platform/v2/x402/discovery/resources` and the PayAI catalog at `https://facilitator.payai.network/discovery/resources`. For Solana-payable services there is also [pay.sh](https://pay.sh), the Solana Foundation's curated catalog.\n\n## Examples\n",
